  "notes": [
    "Reference budgets only; they are not currently enforced by CI.",
    "Fresh timings use isolated empty output directories and allocations are more stable than wall time.",
    "Cache-hit timing is sensitive to filesystem metadata cache state and concurrent disk activity; maximum values intentionally cover the observed noisy range.",
    "Worker timings are aggregate work across up to eight workers and are not additive wall-clock phases.",
    "GitHub is the durable in-repository large-spec workload; App Store Connect is an external comparative workload pinned by repository commit and spec hash.",
    "Both optimized outputs were byte-for-byte identical to CLI 0.32.1-dev.16 for all 41837 generated files.",
    "The Microsoft.OpenApi 3.10.2 verification generated 45582 files byte-for-byte identical to public CLI 0.32.1-dev.27.",
    "The current GitHub verification uses an externally pinned official specification because it is newer and larger than specs/github.yaml.",
    "Parsing subphase budgets use the durable in-repository GitHub workload and the pinned App Store Connect workload; CLI values include cold-process startup and workload-specific post-processing options.",
    "Post-processing detail keeps its aggregate metric for compatibility and records nested phases whose wall times include a small amount of measurement overhead.",
    "The OpenAPI 3.1 compatibility boundary is based on direct Microsoft.OpenApi 3.10.2 reader probes and should be reevaluated on every major reader upgrade.",
    "The enum-render thresholds use three-run medians for the optimized CLI; the public baseline is retained for comparison and wall time remains sensitive to concurrent machine load."
